  "summary": "Ten published items and one preprint, mostly Mendelian randomization and genomic SEM across non-neurodegenerative traits. None address Alzheimer's disease.",
  "synthesis": "The set contains no Alzheimer's disease items despite the topic label; the activity is dominated by statistical genetics applied to other traits. Published work includes Mendelian randomization of latent epigenetic ageing with heel bone mineral density via monocyte genes (IFT80 prioritised), cell-stratified MR linking colorectal cancer liability to thrombosis via PBMC eQTLs, and MR of cis-pQTLs for angina (LPA, PCSK9, APOA5). Genomic SEM appears in adipose ageing, metabolic bone disease and insulin resistance analyses, and a multitrait GWAS links mental disorders to heart failure. The single preprint reanalyses whole-blood RNA-seq in undernutrition and latent tuberculosis without consistent prediction of progression. Signals show a rise ratio of 2.07, with no code, industry or star activity in the window. The items do not establish why activity rose, so the increase is described only as observed.",
